# Kelly configuration (.env for the `kelly` command)
# Copy to .env in the repository root, then `chmod 600 .env`. Never commit .env.
# Every `kelly` command reads this file from the repository root, whatever folder
# you run it from. A value exported in the shell overrides it.
# Full walkthrough: SETUP.md.

# Profile (automatically set by bin/kelly.mjs, but you can override)
# AGENT_PROFILE=kelly

# Trade pack: fixed per install, chosen at setup
KELLY_TRADE=electrical  # electrical | boutique, fixed per install, chosen at setup
# Shop name shown on the dashboard and spoken in the Talk greeting. Set it BEFORE
# importing a boutique rate card: rows without a brand are stored under this name.
# KELLY_SHOP_NAME=Your Shop

# Data and memory directories: catalogue, quotes, designs, logins, settings, memory.
# Unset = ~/.kelly/data and ~/.kelly/memory, which EVERY Kelly checkout for this macOS
# user shares. Only one Kelly on this Mac: leave them unset. More than one (a second
# shop, a test clone): REQUIRED, and unique per install; set both before running any
# `kelly` command. ~/ expands to the home directory; relative paths resolve from the
# repository root. A value exported in the shell overrides this file.
# KELLY_DATA_DIR=~/.kelly-second-shop/data
# KELLY_MEMORY_DIR=~/.kelly-second-shop/memory

# Dashboard. It always binds to 127.0.0.1 (`kelly start` enforces it); tablets
# reach it through a tunnel (see Remote access below).
KELLY_HOST=127.0.0.1
KELLY_PORT=7338
# KELLY_DASHBOARD_TOKEN=optional-security-token
# KELLY_ALLOW_REMOTE_DASHBOARD=0

# Provider: Kelly is Codex-only. The provider is forced to codex in code and
# there is no Claude option or fallback. Sign in with `codex login`.
# KELLY_PROVIDER=codex
# Override the Codex model names only if the owner's Codex account rejects the
# defaults (main, fast worker, deep work):
# KELLY_CODEX_MODEL=
# KELLY_CODEX_T0_MODEL=
# KELLY_CODEX_T2_MODEL=

# Quotation data
# Kelly's knowledge base for quotation patterns
KELLY_KNOWLEDGE_DIR=knowledge/kelly

# Local speech (SETUP.md section 5). Kelly never downloads models or installs
# software: download the three model files into data/voice/models/ yourself.
# `kelly start` finds those files and whisper-cli on PATH on its own; setting the
# paths here also lets `kelly voice status`, `kelly voice transcribe`, and
# Telegram voice notes use them. Relative paths resolve from the repository root.
# Speech to text: whisper.cpp (`brew install whisper.cpp`) + multilingual small q5_1.
# KELLY_WHISPER_CPP_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/whisper-cli
# KELLY_WHISPER_MODEL_PATH=data/voice/models/ggml-small-q5_1.bin
# Text to speech: Kokoro-82M through the kokoro-onnx worker on loopback port 8765.
# The token (24+ characters) is shared by the dashboard and the worker. Generate it
# with: echo "KELLY_KOKORO_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
# If unset, `kelly start` makes a temporary token for each run.
# KELLY_KOKORO_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
# KELLY_KOKORO_TOKEN=
# KELLY_TTS_ENGINE=kokoro
# Python 3.12 venv with scripts/voice/requirements.txt installed; this is the default.
# KELLY_VOICE_PYTHON=data/voice/venv/bin/python
# KELLY_KOKORO_MODEL_PATH=data/voice/models/kokoro-v1.0.int8.onnx
# KELLY_KOKORO_VOICES_PATH=data/voice/models/voices-v1.0.bin
# Only if speech fails with a /Users/runner/work/... phontab error (SETUP.md section 15):
# an absolute path to a copy of espeak-ng-data whose full path is under 160 characters.
# The worker normally handles this on its own.
# KELLY_ESPEAK_DATA_PATH=
# Optional lightweight, robotic fallback: espeak-ng (no model download).
# KELLY_TTS_ENGINE=espeak-ng
# KELLY_TTS_EXECUTABLE=/opt/homebrew/bin/espeak-ng

# Telegram owner voice notes (optional)
# Requires Telegram below, local Whisper above, and an existing ffmpeg binary.
# Kelly never installs ffmpeg or downloads speech models automatically.
# KELLY_FFMPEG_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffmpeg
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_VOICE=1
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_VOICE_MAX_BYTES=20971520
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_VOICE_MAX_SECONDS=300
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_VOICE_LANGUAGE=auto
# Optional: send short spoken answers after the normal text answer.
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_VOICE_REPLIES=0

# Counter tablet mode: review (default) | conversation | talk. `talk` is the
# hands-free Talk page. Usually set in the dashboard's Voice pane; a valid value
# here overrides the saved setting.
# KELLY_COUNTER_MODE=talk

# Telegram notifications (optional; leave empty to disable). SETUP.md section 13.
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-bot-token
# KELLY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your-chat-id

# Email (intentionally not configured for Kelly)
# Kelly does not support Gmail integration by design

# Remote access (optional: a shop tablet reaching this Mac's dashboard, or a public
# demo link). Kelly's dashboard always binds to 127.0.0.1; this only starts a tunnel
# process that forwards into that loopback address.
# See docs/modules/remote-access.md.
# KELLY_TUNNEL=off               off (default) | tailscale | cloudflare | funnel
#   tailscale: tailnet-only (Tailscale Serve); the tablet must join the same tailnet.
#   funnel:    public (Tailscale Funnel); anyone with the link can reach the login page.
#   cloudflare: public link on your own domain (set up with `kelly tunnel setup`).
# `kelly start` ignores KELLY_TUNNEL and sets it from its flags: no --public = off,
# --public tailscale = tailscale (Serve), --public cloudflare = cloudflare, bare
# --public = cloudflare when KELLY_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL is set, otherwise funnel.
# `kelly dashboard` alone uses the value set here.
# KELLY_TAILSCALE_PATH=tailscale         path to the tailscale binary (also tried at
#                                         /Applications/Tailscale.app/Contents/MacOS/Tailscale)
# KELLY_CLOUDFLARED_PATH=cloudflared     path to the cloudflared binary
# KELLY_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL=kelly-shop     named tunnel to run (required for cloudflare mode)
# KELLY_PUBLIC_HOST=kelly.your-domain.com   the public hostname for a Cloudflare tunnel; used
#                                         for the printed status URL and as the trusted origin
#                                         (KELLY_PUBLIC_ORIGIN) unless that is set explicitly.
#                                         `kelly tunnel setup <hostname>` writes this for you.
# KELLY_TUNNEL_PORT=                     defaults to KELLY_PORT

# The public link ("Explore Kelly"). Through any tunnel (Cloudflare, Funnel, or Tailscale Serve)
# an unauthenticated visitor sees ONLY the Explore page and its three conversation modes (talk,
# counter, chat), answered by a tool-less, sandboxed Kelly that never sees or saves your real
# conversations, transcripts, memory, quotes, activity, approvals, usage, or settings.
# See docs/public-explore.md.
# KELLY_REMOTE_LOGIN=off                 on = the owner and counter logins work through the tunnel
#                                         again (needed for a shop tablet on a tunnel link).
#                                         Off by default: the tunnel has no login page at all.
# KELLY_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://kelly.your-domain.com   exact https origin visitors' pages post from
#                                         (defaults to https://<KELLY_PUBLIC_HOST>)
# KELLY_PUBLIC_SHOP_NAME=                shop name shown to visitors (defaults to KELLY_SHOP_NAME)
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS=1000    longest visitor message
# KELLY_PUBLIC_HISTORY_TURNS=20          turns remembered per visitor, in memory only
# KELLY_PUBLIC_IDLE_MINUTES=15           an idle visitor's conversation is forgotten
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_VISITORS=500          visitors held in memory at once
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_CONCURRENT=2          public model turns at once (the rest queue, then get a busy line)
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_QUEUE=4
# KELLY_PUBLIC_QUEUE_WAIT_SECONDS=25
# KELLY_PUBLIC_TURN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# KELLY_PUBLIC_VISITOR_PER_MINUTE=6      per-visitor turn limits
# KELLY_PUBLIC_VISITOR_PER_HOUR=60
# KELLY_PUBLIC_CLIENT_PER_MINUTE=12      per-client limits (Cloudflare's client address, rate limits only)
# KELLY_PUBLIC_CLIENT_PER_HOUR=120
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_AUDIO_BYTES=2000000   longest recording a visitor may upload
# KELLY_PUBLIC_MAX_AUDIO_SECONDS=30
# KELLY_PUBLIC_TIER=t1                   t0 | t1 | t2 model tier for public turns
# KELLY_PUBLIC_REQUEST_LOG=on            content-free request log at <KELLY_DATA_DIR>/logs/public.log

# Security
KELLY_REQUIRE_OUTBOUND_APPROVAL=1

# Performance
KELLY_BROWSER_HEADLESS=1

# Cross-site origins allowed to read /api/health (for example a status badge on
# your own website), comma-separated. Default empty: no cross-site reads.
# KELLY_HEALTH_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-domain.com

# Owner email (optional)
# KELLY_OWNER_EMAIL=your-email@example.com

# Owner name (optional): used in runtime prompts, messages, and UI text.
# Defaults to "the owner" when unset.
# KELLY_OWNER_NAME=your-name
